+- [x] 1.2 In `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py`, make the end request's socket-inactivity budget host-aware per design D1 — codex 2.0 s, claude 3.0 s — with a comment naming the 3-second Codex clamp it serves; then verify by running `python -m unittest test_session_hook.test_session_hook.SessionHookTests.test_end_accepts_slow_matching_ack_without_extra_posts` from the `plugins/graphhelm/hooks` directory (the ~1.25 s Codex slow-ack case must still deliver).
+
+## 2. Mirror the `graphhelm-codex-hooks` companion
+
+- [x] 2.1 Apply the identical edits to `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/codex-hooks.json` and replace `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/session_hook.py` with the exact bytes of the updated primary copies, then verify with `python -m unittest test_session_hook.test_session_hook.SessionHookTests.test_codex_compatibility_package_keeps_one_hook_source` from the `plugins/graphhelm/hooks` directory (byte-identity holds).
+
+## 3. Correct the README budget paragraph
+
+- [x] 3.1 Rewrite the budget paragraph in `plugins/graphhelm/README.md` (currently lines 57–61, "Both hosts bound the SessionEnd command process to five seconds") to state per-host facts per design D3 — Claude Code bounds both events at 5 s; Codex declares 5 for `SessionStart` and 3 for `SessionEnd`, matching the host clamp; in-request limits are 1 s of socket inactivity for `SessionStart` and up to 3 s (Claude) / 2 s (Codex) for `SessionEnd` — keeping the existing "not a wall-time deadline" and "timeout remains unobserved" wording, then verify by re-reading the paragraph alongside both manifests and the script and confirming every stated number matches the code.
+
+## 4. Full hook-suite integration check
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run the complete suite from `plugins/graphhelm/hooks`: `python -m unittest test_session_hook -v`, verify every test passes with no test-file modifications (`git status --porcelain` shows no diff in `test_session_hook.py`) and `git diff --name-only` lists exactly the four intended files plus `README.md`.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Verification note (unattended run, 2026-10-26): the unittest paths written in tasks 1.2 and 2.1
+  (`test_session_hook.test_session_hook.SessionHookTests...`) name a nested module that does not
+  exist in this checkout — `test_session_hook.py` is a single-file module, so those paths fail at
+  load with an AttributeError independent of any code change. Both verifications were therefore run
+  from `plugins/graphhelm/hooks` with the resolved path `test_session_hook.SessionHookTests.<test>`;
+  the observed behavior each task names (slow-ack delivery, byte identity) held.
+
+- Archive the change (`openspec archive bench-feature`) after the project's review requirements are satisfied.
+- Verify the archived result (the `session-hooks` capability appears under `openspec/specs/`).
